  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest Effect Fund TA: &#x201c;Fund-in-fund management company start-up phase support&#x201d;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Forest Effect Fund (FEF) is a Dutch private equity fund, part of the Dutch Good Growth Fund. The Fund focusses on entrepreneurs active in the agri-commodity and food chains of coffee, cacao, nuts, fruits and palm oil in developing countries and emerging markets.In addition to making good returns on investment, the purpose of the fund is to generate local &apos;impact&apos; measurable in terms of job creation, knowledge transfer and production growth in the agri-commodity chains.Technical Assistance through DGGF-TA was provided to help to set-up the fund and to enhance the development impact and long term viability of the FEF. This included portfolio and market development, the set-up of internal organisational processes and Report and  impact measurement on deals and deal flow. The fund is now fully operational and has already supported 3 companies with their impact investments.</narrative>
  </description>
